WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.504
The saved Week 9 reading table has eleven rows. Each row has a book or source, chapter/page locator, learning outcome, and focus. This guide keeps those rows separate rather than merging similar-looking titles.
学校保存的第9周阅读表有十一条记录；每条都有书名或来源、章节页码、学习成果和重点。本指南保留各条目，不把相似标题合并。

00:00:15.504 --> 00:00:28.512
A bilingual explanation is a study aid, not a replacement for the assigned pages. When the saved school edition cannot be matched to a local candidate text, the mismatch is stated rather than hidden.
双语讲解是学习辅助，不替代指定页码。若学校版本无法与本地候选教材匹配，会明确说明差异，不会掩盖。

00:00:28.512 --> 00:00:41.568
The week joins two explicitly allocated modules, 5B Operational Safety and 7F Environmental Pathophysiology. Readings support those modules and the school’s practical stations.
本周连接两个明确安排的模块：5B行动安全与7F环境病理生理。指定阅读为这些模块及学校实操站点提供支持。

00:00:41.568 --> 00:00:56.256
A&P and CV Patho help explain blood flow, oxygen pressure and ECG effects. MSN, CNS and VSM add assessment and measurement concepts; they do not all refer to the same edition.
A&P与CV Patho帮助解释血流、氧分压及心电变化；MSN、CNS与VSM增加评估和测量概念，但这些教材并非同一版本。

00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:08.952
BCEHS and BCPEG do not have the same function. One is the current service guideline; the other is the school-assigned dated examination snapshot. Keep both visible when they differ.
BCEHS与BCPEG功能不同：前者是现行服务指南，后者是学校指定的有日期考试快照。存在差异时，两者都要保留。

00:01:08.952 --> 00:01:22.800
FON and PMHN explain stress and grief in a nursing education context. Use their concepts to support humane communication without diagnosing a patient or assuming a required emotional response.
FON与PMHN从护理教育角度解释应激及哀伤。可用其概念支持有人文关怀的沟通，但不能据此诊断患者或假设其必须作出某种情绪反应。

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:54.600
The recovered AET-folder A and P copy resolves the earlier altitude page mismatch. Its printed pages 981 to 983 really contain respiratory adaptation and altitude, followed by the opening of respiratory development. The full assigned circulation range also includes fetal pathways and its first key-terms page. The older public candidate remains a different pagination, not evidence that the actual assigned pages are missing.
找回的AET文件夹A&P副本解决了先前高海拔页码不符；其印刷981至983页确实包含呼吸适应与高海拔，随后开始呼吸发育。完整指定循环范围还含胎儿路径及第一张关键词页。较旧公共候选本仍是不同页码，不能据此认定实际指定页缺失。

00:01:54.600 --> 00:02:17.832
The identified school-folder cardiovascular book has seventy-nine physical pages, so the assigned pages one hundred eighty-one through one hundred eighty-three cannot occur in that file. The reader explains its named calcium and J-wave content with this locator difference visible. An identified topic is not literal page equivalence, and no missing page is silently invented.
已识别的学校文件夹心血管教材只有79个实际页，所以其中不可能存在指定181至183页。读本讲解其点名的钙及J波内容，并明确保留定位差异。找到主题不等于指定页完全对应，也不能悄悄编造缺页。

00:02:17.832 --> 00:02:47.784
The recovered CNS, CPSC and PHARM course copies now anchor their literal assigned spans. In the actual PHARM copy, pages 588 to 592 really contain antiplatelets, and the full assigned Chapter 22 review includes the later shock-drug material. The earlier candidate pagination conflict is resolved, not retained as a gap. Nursing-source treatment examples still do not expand PCP authority.
找回的CNS、CPSC及PHARM课程副本，现成为其实际指定范围的依据。实际PHARM中588至592页确实包含抗血小板药，完整指定第22章复习也包含后面的休克药内容。先前候选页码冲突已经解决，不再当成缺口保留。护理来源治疗示例仍不会扩大PCP权限。

00:02:47.784 --> 00:03:00.072
The saved school outline asks for a 60-second tourniquet competency and a 30-second load-and-go verbal decision. These are school station targets, not universal clinical deadlines.
学校保存的纲要要求60秒止血带考核及30秒装车决策口述；这是学校站点目标，不是通用临床时限。

00:03:00.072 --> 00:03:18.912
Current BCEHS H09, H10, H12, H02, I01, I02 and N04 provide service-specific clinical guidance. Use the applicable current pathway, including its consultation and provider-level requirements.
BCEHS现行H09、H10、H12、H02、I01、I02及N04提供服务特定的临床指导。应使用适用的现行路径，包括咨询及执业层级要求。

00:03:18.912 --> 00:03:40.200
The lesson now distinguishes the actual March 31, 2025 BCPEG course copy from the later June 15, 2026 comparison and current service guidance. Their doses, headings and thresholds are not silently merged into one action card. The instructor-assessed revision remains a separate question.
本课现在区分实际2025年3月31日BCPEG课程副本、较后2026年6月15日比较版，以及机构现行指导。不能把其剂量、标题及阈值悄悄合并成一张操作卡。教师考核采用哪一修订版，仍须另行确认。

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:51.720
For each row, first locate the assigned source. Then identify what the page teaches and what it does not teach. Page presence alone is not comprehension.
每项阅读先打开指定来源，再辨别该页教了什么、没有教什么。页码存在不代表已经理解。

00:03:51.720 --> 00:04:03.984
After reading, explain the concept in your own English words, then restate it in Chinese while preserving the key English term. This helps prepare both for English course language and bilingual review.
读完后先用自己的英文解释概念，再用中文复述，同时保留关键英文术语。这有助于适应英文课程语言和双语复习。

00:04:03.984 --> 00:04:16.608
Finish with a new application question: what would change your concern, next assessment or escalation? Do not memorize a nursing action or older protocol as independent PCP authority.
最后用新情景检索：什么发现会改变你的担忧、下一项评估或升级行动？不要把护理措施或旧规程背成PCP独立授权。

00:04:16.608 --> 00:04:33.024
The Kubler-Ross vocabulary is denial, anger, bargaining, depression and acceptance. Learn the English names for the reading, but do not turn them into five compulsory steps, a timetable or a grading system for a family’s response.
Kubler-Ross词汇包括denial、anger、bargaining、depression及acceptance。阅读时要学会英文名称，但不能把它们变为五个必经步骤、时间表，或给家属反应评分的系统。

00:04:33.024 --> 00:04:51.120
The text rejects several unrealistic expectations: everyone following the same order, finishing by a deadline or expressing emotion in the same way. Support an individual response and the person’s chosen connections rather than imposing your own idea of correct grieving.
原文否定多种不现实期待：人人依同一顺序、在期限前结束，或用相同方式表达情绪。应支持个人反应及其选择的联系，而不是强加自己对正确哀伤的看法。

00:04:51.120 --> 00:05:13.008
Emotional effects can include fear, sadness, guilt, regret, anger or relief, sometimes together. Social effects may include changed roles, loneliness and strained relationships. None of these observations proves how much a person cared or establishes a psychiatric diagnosis on its own.
情绪影响可包括恐惧、悲伤、内疚、遗憾、愤怒或释然，有时同时出现。社会影响可包括角色改变、孤独及关系紧张。这些观察都不能证明本人在乎多少，也不能单独确立精神科诊断。

00:05:13.008 --> 00:05:36.264
The reading discusses losses experienced by nurses and the effects of repeated exposure. For an EMS learner, connect this to fatigue, sleep, readiness, boundaries and access to confidential support. Burnout, compassion fatigue and traumatic stress are related concerns, not interchangeable diagnoses from one difficult shift.
阅读讨论护理人员经历的丧失及反复接触影响。EMS学习者可联系疲劳、睡眠、履职准备、边界及保密支持。职业耗竭、共情疲劳与创伤应激是相关问题，但不能凭一次困难班次互换诊断。

00:05:36.264 --> 00:06:10.152
Original rehearsal: following a drowning resuscitation, a partner repeats the same question and a friend stands silently nearby. The patient is being transported and the outcome is not yet known. Say what is confirmed, without predicting death or recovery: the team is treating the patient and transporting them for further care. Pause, ask what the partner understood, and ask whom they would like contacted. Include the chosen friend if the partner wants that support; silence does not mean the friend is unaffected.
原创演练：溺水复苏后，伴侣反复问同一个问题，一位朋友安静站在旁边。患者正被转运，结局尚不明确。只说已确认事实，不预测死亡或康复：团队正在救治患者，并转运接受进一步照护。停顿，询问伴侣理解了什么，以及希望联系谁。若伴侣愿意，可让其选择的朋友提供支持；沉默不表示朋友未受影响。

00:06:10.152 --> 00:06:44.832
Worked reasoning: repeated questions can reflect difficulty processing information, so use short statements and check understanding rather than assigning a denial stage. Offer practical help without promising a clinical outcome. If either person develops chest pain, breathing difficulty, collapse or another acute concern, assess that problem on its own merits. For retrieval, explain one secondary loss, one way social recognition changes support, and one statement that is both truthful and compassionate in this case.
推理示范：反复提问可能反映难以处理信息，因此应使用简短陈述并检查理解，而不是认定处于否认阶段。可提供实际帮助，但不能承诺临床结局。若任何一人出现胸痛、呼吸困难、倒地或其他急性问题，应按问题本身评估。提取练习：说明一个次级丧失、社会承认怎样影响支持，以及在本情境中一句既真实又有同理心的话。

00:06:44.832 --> 00:07:08.016
For physiology, distinguish two coordinated arms: sympathetic/adrenal activity contributes to rapid catecholamine responses, while the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis regulates cortisol. The book paragraph compresses these into one chain; its own diagram separates nerves to the medulla from hormonal signaling to the cortex.
生理上要区分两条协调途径：交感及肾上腺活动参与快速儿茶酚胺反应，下丘脑-垂体-肾上腺轴调节皮质醇。教材段落把它们压缩成单一链，但其自身图示将通向髓质的神经与通向皮质的激素信号分开。

00:07:08.016 --> 00:07:30.168
The HPA sequence is hypothalamic CRH, pituitary ACTH and adrenal-cortex cortisol. NIDDK and the NIOSH review support this distinction from the sympathetic arm. Do not learn ACTH as a switch that directly accounts for every sympathetic effect, or infer a hormone concentration from a pulse rate.
HPA顺序是下丘脑CRH、垂体ACTH及肾上腺皮质皮质醇。NIDDK及NIOSH综述支持将其与交感途径区分。不能把ACTH背成直接解释全部交感效应的开关，也不能从脉率推断激素浓度。

00:07:30.168 --> 00:07:51.696
General adaptation syndrome refers here to a whole-body stress response; local adaptation syndrome concerns a more regional response. The assigned section names GAS and points to 34.4 for deeper theory. Do not substitute an extensive unassigned GAS-stage lecture for the actual local-response content on these pages.
本范围中的一般适应综合征指全身应激反应；局部适应综合征关注区域性反应。指定节介绍GAS，并指向34.4深入理论。不能用大量未指定的GAS阶段课程，替代这些页面实际的局部反应内容。

00:07:51.696 --> 00:08:12.528
The inflammatory example uses redness, swelling, warmth, pain and loss of function. A local response can help contain harm, while excessive or persistent inflammation can also cause problems. These signs do not by themselves prove infection, and absence of one does not exclude a serious condition.
炎症例子包括发红、肿胀、温热、疼痛及功能丧失。局部反应可帮助限制伤害，但过度或持续炎症也可带来问题。这些体征本身不证明感染，缺少其中之一也不能排除严重情况。

00:08:12.528 --> 00:08:52.128
Original rehearsal: during a prolonged extrication, a trainee reports trembling hands, a racing heart and difficulty concentrating. One teammate calls this adrenal exhaustion. Identify the actual demands instead: heat, protective equipment, a difficult scene, repeated alarms, workload and possible inadequate rest. Symptoms alone cannot establish a hormone level, an exhaustion stage or a psychological cause. Communicate the difficulty to the supervisor, arrange safe task coverage and assess any acute illness or injury as indicated.
原创演练：长时间解救被困者时，一名学员报告手抖、心跳快及难以集中注意力。一名队友称这是肾上腺耗竭。应先识别实际要求：高温、防护装备、困难现场、反复警报、工作量，以及可能休息不足。仅凭症状不能确定激素水平、衰竭阶段或心理病因。应向主管沟通困难、安排安全的任务接替，并按指征评估急性疾病或损伤。

00:08:52.128 --> 00:09:29.544
Worked reasoning: the sympathetic arm and the HPA axis are coordinated but distinct. The first concerns rapid neural and catecholamine responses; the second involves hypothalamic CRH, pituitary ACTH and adrenal-cortex cortisol. Neither can be measured from the trainee's pulse alone. Name a feasible immediate support and a reassessment, then a recovery or confidential-support option after the scene. Do not require the trainee to disclose personal experiences publicly, and do not use a theory label to certify readiness for a hazardous task.
推理示范：交感途径与HPA轴协调但不同。前者涉及快速神经及儿茶酚胺反应；后者涉及下丘脑CRH、垂体ACTH及肾上腺皮质皮质醇。两者都不能只凭学员脉率测定。先说出一个可行的即时支持及复评，再说出现场结束后的恢复或保密支持选项。不能要求学员公开披露个人经历，也不能用理论标签证明其适合执行危险任务。

00:09:29.544 --> 00:09:54.120
Anemia illustrates saturation versus oxygen delivery: the available hemoglobin can be well saturated while its total quantity is inadequate. Hypovolemia can reduce flow despite a preserved saturation value. Assess breathing, perfusion, mental status, symptoms and trends together; SpO2 alone measures neither blood volume nor cardiac output.
贫血说明饱和度与供氧的差别：现有血红蛋白可高度饱和，但总量不足。低血容量可在饱和度保留时仍减少血流。应综合呼吸、灌注、意识、症状及趋势；SpO2单独既不测血容量，也不测心输出量。

00:09:54.120 --> 00:10:28.656
Original case: after a cold-water rescue, a patient is pale, breathing rapidly and becoming confused. A finger probe flickers between ninety-six and ninety-nine percent while a cuff is cycling on that arm. Assess the patient immediately; separate the conflicting measurements, inspect signal quality and use an approved suitable site. Reassess breathing, circulation, mental status and pressure using a documented method. A better-looking saturation number does not explain away the deterioration.
原创情境：冷水救援后，患者苍白、呼吸快，意识逐渐混乱。指端探头在96%-99%间闪动，同侧手臂袖带正循环充气。应立即评估患者，分开互相干扰的测量，检查信号质量，并采用获准的合适部位。以有记录的方法复评呼吸、循环、意识及血压。更好看的饱和度数字不能解释掉恶化。

00:10:28.656 --> 00:10:57.456
Before an auscultatory reading, estimate systolic pressure by palpation while inflating until the radial or brachial pulse disappears. The source teaches a maximum inflation pressure thirty millimeters of mercury above the disappearance point. This is not thirty above an assumed normal pressure. A silent auscultatory gap can otherwise make the later reappearance of sound look like the first systolic sound, falsely lowering the recorded systolic value.
听诊测量前，应在充气时触诊，直到桡或肱动脉脉搏消失，以估计收缩压。来源教导的最高充气压是消失点以上30毫米汞柱，不是猜测正常压力后再加30。否则听诊间隙的暂时无声，可使后来再次出现的声音被误当作首次收缩音，令所记收缩压假低。

00:10:57.456 --> 00:11:28.512
In the source two-step method, first determine that inflation level and release the cuff, then position the stethoscope, reinflate to the determined level and deflate evenly at about two millimeters of mercury per second. Identify the first Korotkoff sound as systolic and final disappearance as diastolic, then fully release pressure and record the result. Use supervised practice and the applicable measurement procedure; text alone does not establish auscultatory skill.
来源的两步法是：先确定充气水平并放气，再放置听诊器，重新充到已确定水平，以约每秒2毫米汞柱均匀放气。首次柯氏音为收缩压，最终消失为舒张压；之后完全放气并记录结果。应接受指导下练习并采用适用测量流程；文字本身不能证明听诊技能。

00:11:28.512 --> 00:11:56.256
Troubleshoot systematically if a brachial pulse or sound is difficult to find: confirm anatomy, arm position, reasonable palpation pressure, chestpiece position and selected side, seal, earpiece fit and surrounding noise. Pressing too hard can obliterate a pulse. Reposition or use another appropriate method, stating a limitation if necessary; do not enter a guessed value merely to fill the chart.
难以找到肱动脉脉搏或声音时，应系统排查：解剖位置、手臂体位、合适触诊力度、听诊面位置及开启侧、接触、耳塞贴合和环境噪音。过度按压可使脉搏消失。必要时重新定位或使用其他适用方法，并说明限制；不能为填表而猜一个数值。

00:11:56.256 --> 00:12:36.000
Worked retrieval: explain why cold and cuff inflation can degrade the signal, why saturation is not total oxygen delivery, and why a preserved systolic pressure cannot exclude hypoperfusion. Then rehearse choosing the cuff, supporting the arm, estimating inflation by palpation, identifying sounds and documenting a trend. Compare an original reading of one hundred twelve over seventy-four with a later ninety-four over sixty-eight only after checking method and conditions; their pulse pressures are thirty-eight and twenty-six, but the patient and trajectory determine concern, not subtraction alone.
提取示范：解释冷及袖带充气为何可削弱信号、饱和度为何不等于总供氧，以及保留的收缩压为何不能排除低灌注。再演练选择袖带、支撑手臂、触诊估计充气水平、识别声音及记录趋势。核查方法及条件后，再比较初始112/74与后来94/68；脉压分别38及26，但担忧程度由患者与变化过程决定，不是单靠减法。

00:12:36.000 --> 00:13:07.344
The actual page 162 adds culturally safe consent. Explain information accessibly, avoid coercion, seek consent before a procedure where feasible and respect the person's ability to withdraw it. Ask whether an Elder, Knowledge Keeper or chosen advocate would help rather than assigning a preference from identity. Historical and current power imbalances are reasons to improve communication and choice, not assume that an Indigenous patient cannot understand or decide.
实际162页增加文化安全的同意要求。应以易懂方式解释信息，避免胁迫，可行时在操作前征求同意，并尊重本人撤回同意。可以询问长者、知识传承者或本人选择的倡导者是否有帮助，而不是按身份指定偏好。历史及当前权力失衡，意味着要改善沟通与选择，不意味着假定原住民患者不能理解或决定。

00:13:07.344 --> 00:13:38.568
The same literal page requires assessment with consent, decision-specific capacity assessment, discussion of risks and a specific worsening-symptom plan. A referral must be accepted or follow the established process, with clear follow-up and documentation; a phone number alone is not a completed referral. FR autonomous non-conveyance is excluded, and pediatric or police-custody non-conveyance requires CliniCall. A signature does not replace the clinical reasoning or a workable plan.
同一实际页要求经同意评估、针对具体决定评估能力、讨论风险，并制定明确的症状恶化方案。转介须获接收或依既定流程，并有清楚随访及记录；仅给电话号码不等于完成转介。FR不适用自主非转运；儿科或警方羁押患者的非转运需要CliniCall。签名不能替代临床推理或可行方案。

00:13:38.568 --> 00:14:12.384
Original rehearsal: a six-year-old is pulled from a garden pond and is now awake but coughing. A caregiver wants to leave because the child is speaking. Establish the event timeline and assess breathing, oxygenation, temperature and injuries, while explaining why speaking does not exclude evolving lung injury. Use the pediatric pathway and required consultation for a non-conveyance decision. Invite the caregiver's questions and check understanding rather than describing the request itself as incapacity.
原创演练：六岁儿童从花园池塘救出，现清醒但咳嗽。照护者因儿童能说话而想离开。应明确事件时间线，评估呼吸、氧合、体温及损伤，并解释能说话不排除肺损伤进展。应采用儿科路径，并在非转运决定中进行要求的咨询。邀请照护者提问并检查理解，不能仅因其提出离开就描述为无决定能力。

00:14:12.384 --> 00:14:49.632
Worked reasoning: water safety comes before contact; then effective breathing and a complete assessment guide urgency. Explain confirmed findings and the risk of delayed change, without inventing a prognosis or guaranteeing that observation will be harmless. Document findings, advice, consultation, the person's understanding and the actual agreed disposition. For retrieval, contrast immersion with submersion and assisted breaths with CPAP, then explain why an A09 page in the assigned span cannot silently be renamed A08.
推理示范：接触前先确保水域安全；之后由有效呼吸及完整评估指导紧急程度。应解释已确认发现及延迟变化风险，不编造预后，也不保证观察绝无问题。记录发现、建议、咨询、对方理解及实际商定去向。提取练习：对比immersion与submersion、辅助呼吸与CPAP，再解释为何不能把指定范围内A09页面悄悄改名为A08。

00:14:49.632 --> 00:15:17.424
Traumatic arrest commonly reflects severe blood loss, inadequate oxygenation or obstructed circulation. A heart may show organized electrical activity without enough filling or forward flow to produce a palpable pulse. Simultaneously addressing hemorrhage, oxygenation and relevant obstruction targets the mechanism; chest compressions alone cannot replace missing circulating volume or release a tension pneumothorax.
创伤骤停常涉及严重失血、氧合不足或循环梗阻。心脏可有有组织电活动，却因充盈或前向血流不足而摸不到脉搏。同时处理出血、氧合及相关梗阻，是针对机制；仅胸外按压不能替代缺失循环容量，也不能解除张力性气胸。

00:15:17.424 --> 00:15:46.104
The general N04 discussion describes chest decompression, but its intervention ladder places bilateral needle thoracentesis in ACP care and additional invasive or blood-product actions at higher levels. Read a general paragraph together with the role-specific procedure, not as expanded PCP permission. A team should identify the suspected threat, request the appropriate resource and avoid delaying other indicated treatment while waiting.
N04一般讨论提到胸部减压，但层级干预将双侧针刺胸腔减压列入ACP照护，并将其他侵入性或血制品措施置于更高层级。阅读一般段落时必须同时查按角色限定的流程，不能视为扩大PCP权限。团队应识别疑似威胁、请求适当资源，等待时仍不延误其他有指征处理。

00:15:46.104 --> 00:16:17.304
Page 20 concerns preservation of an amputated part, not initial tourniquet placement. Stabilize the patient and control life-threatening bleeding before spending time on the separated tissue. Preserve the possibility of reattachment without treating the part as more urgent than breathing, circulation or safe conveyance. The school's separate sixty-second tourniquet competency measures timely complete bleeding control and recording, not how quickly the amputated part is packed.
第20页讲断肢保存，不是初始止血带放置。先稳定患者、控制致命出血，再花时间处理离体组织。应保留再植可能，但不能把断肢置于呼吸、循环或安全转运之前。学校另设的60秒止血带考核，衡量及时完全止血及记录，不是断肢包装速度。

00:16:17.304 --> 00:16:44.472
Do not warm the amputated part, immerse it in water, place it directly on ice or use dry ice. Distinguish a brief cleaning rinse from leaving tissue submerged, and indirect cooling through protection from direct freezing contact. Preserve identification and convey the part with the patient. Do not attempt reattachment in a classroom rehearsal or delay urgent patient care while searching indefinitely for missing tissue.
不能加热断肢、浸泡水中、直接放冰上或用干冰。应区分短暂清洁冲洗与持续浸泡，以及隔层保护下间接冷却与直接冻伤接触。保持身份对应，断肢随患者转运。课堂演练不尝试再植，也不能为无限寻找缺失组织而拖延患者急救。

00:16:44.472 --> 00:17:17.136
On page 54, hypovolemia means evidence of a significant loss of blood or body fluid, connected to poor tissue perfusion. The source lists systolic pressure below ninety and other shock findings, but its footnote allows use above ninety when the mechanism, injuries or condition suggest impending shock. Therefore, a still-preserved pressure does not end the assessment. Identify bleeding or fluid loss, repeated findings and trajectory rather than waiting for a number to cross a threshold.
第54页低血容量是有明显血液或体液丧失证据，并连接组织灌注不足。来源列收缩压低于90及其他休克发现，但脚注允许在机制、损伤或状况提示即将休克时于90以上使用。因此血压暂时保留，不代表评估结束。应识别出血或体液丧失、重复发现及变化过程，不能只等数字过阈值。

00:17:17.136 --> 00:17:48.432
Original arithmetic rehearsal, not a patient order: seventy kilograms multiplied by twenty milliliters per kilogram equals fourteen hundred milliliters. The source's five-hundred-milliliter reassessment wording means that a calculated total is not an uninterrupted automatic delivery. Explain what findings would change the plan and which current source authorizes it. A rising pressure alone does not prove restored tissue perfusion, and a fluid calculation does not replace hemorrhage control.
原创算术演练，不是患者医嘱：70公斤乘每公斤20毫升，等于1400毫升。来源每500毫升复评的措辞，意味着算出总量并不等于自动连续输入。应解释什么发现会改变方案，以及依据哪一现行来源授权。血压升高本身不证明组织灌注恢复，补液计算也不能替代止血。

00:17:48.432 --> 00:18:22.032
The actual 2025 table puts epistaxis and postpartum hemorrhage in a medical-oversight-consult-required row. The later 2026 table changes that heading to considerations. That changed label does not itself grant autonomous administration. The current service monograph explicitly requires prior CliniCall for its maternal vaginal-bleeding/postpartum indication; epistaxis is not listed as a current indication there. Keep the exact source and consultation condition attached to the use being discussed.
实际2025表将鼻出血及产后出血放在“须医疗监督咨询”行，较后2026表把标题改成“考虑事项”。标签改变本身不授予自主给药权限。机构现行专论明确要求其母体阴道出血或产后出血适应症先咨询CliniCall；该专论没有把鼻出血列为现行适应症。讨论用途时必须保留确切来源及咨询条件。

00:18:22.032 --> 00:18:56.184
Current service eligibility and exclusions must be read separately: shock or hypoperfusion with suspected injury-related bleeding is the trauma context; nontraumatic gastrointestinal bleeding is excluded, and pediatric age limits differ by provider level. The current monograph does not list isolated TBI in its contraindication list, unlike the examination copy, but absence from that list does not establish an indication when its positive bleeding criteria are absent. Do not average the two lists or silently substitute one for the other.
现行机构资格及排除必须另读：创伤背景是休克或低灌注伴疑似损伤相关出血；非创伤性胃肠出血被排除，儿科年龄限制按提供者层级不同。与考试副本不同，现行专论禁忌表没有列单纯TBI，但未列禁忌不表示在缺乏其正面出血标准时就有适应症。不能把两张表折中平均，也不能悄悄互换。

00:18:56.184 --> 00:19:35.496
The source box labels cue recognition, pattern recognition, problem representation, hypothesis generation, hypothesis evaluation and final judgment as six NCJMM steps. These are not the official six measured functions. NCSBN names recognize cues, analyze cues, prioritize hypotheses, generate solutions, take action and evaluate outcomes. Retain the discrepancy for source-based study instead of memorizing the box as an exact official sequence. Neither model replaces an urgent primary assessment or grants nursing or paramedic authority.
来源框把线索识别、模式识别、问题表征、假设生成、假设评价及最终判断列作NCJMM六步，但这不是官方六项测量功能。NCSBN使用recognize cues、analyze cues、prioritize hypotheses、generate solutions、take action及evaluate outcomes。来源学习时应保留差异，不能把该框背成确切官方顺序。任何模型都不替代紧急初评，也不授予护理或救护员权限。

00:19:35.496 --> 00:20:06.792
Worked reasoning: notice the new pallor, dizziness and reduced participation; interpret possible impaired perfusion without assuming one cause; respond with assessment, indicated support and a safer movement plan; evaluate the response and communicate changes. Keep these actions within actual scope and device instructions. The patient's weight-bearing restriction, current assistance needs and clinical urgency answer three different questions, all of which are needed before the move.
推理示范：发现新苍白、头晕及参与下降；考虑灌注受损而不假定唯一病因；通过评估、有指征支持及较安全搬动方案回应；评价反应并沟通变化。行动仍须遵循真实权限及器材说明。患者负重限制、目前所需协助及临床紧急程度，回答三个不同问题，移动前都需要明确。

00:20:06.792 --> 00:20:40.008
Brake use is device- and phase-specific. The textbook's blanket instruction to lock a wheeled lift conflicts with the manufacturer's Hoyer Advance lifting instruction, which leaves the lift casters unbraked so it can center under the load. That does not mean every bed, wheelchair or lift should be unlocked. Identify the exact device and movement phase, stabilize the receiving surface as required and follow its complete instructions with training; never combine fragments into an invented operating sequence.
刹车使用取决于设备及阶段。教材一概锁住有轮升降器的说法，与Hoyer Advance厂家抬升说明冲突；后者在抬升时让升降器脚轮不制动，以便移到载荷重心下方。这不表示所有床、轮椅或升降器都应解锁。应识别确切设备及移动阶段，按要求稳定接收表面，并经培训遵循完整说明；不能拼凑片段自创操作顺序。

00:20:40.008 --> 00:21:11.304
Distinguish a standard frame, a two-wheeled walker, a four-wheeled rollator and a forearm-support design. A standard frame is lifted and positioned before the next supported step; front wheels can allow advancement without lifting the whole frame. The source paragraph calls the two wheels rear wheels, but its own figure shows front wheels, consistent with HealthLinkBC. A rollator's brakes and seat add their own operating requirements; more wheels do not automatically mean safer support.
应区分标准助行架、双轮助行器、四轮带座助行器及前臂支持设计。标准架先提起放好，再完成下一支撑步；前轮可使移动时不需提起整个架。来源段落把双轮说成后轮，但其自身图示是前轮，与HealthLinkBC一致。四轮器的刹车及座椅另有操作要求；轮子更多不自动表示支持更安全。

00:21:11.304 --> 00:21:45.768
Original rehearsal: a person awaiting movement from a worksite chair says the injured leg must not bear weight. They use a cane at baseline but are now pale, dizzy and less able to follow instructions. Do not use the familiar cane or a previous transfer to justify standing. Reassess the acute change, protect the injured limb, explain the revised plan and obtain appropriate equipment and trained help for a supported move. The route and urgency must reflect the actual condition, not simply the usual walking aid.
原创演练：一名等候从工地椅子搬动的人说伤腿不能负重。平时用手杖，但现在苍白、头晕，较难按指令配合。不能因熟悉的手杖或以前转移成功就决定站立。应复评急性变化、保护伤肢、解释修订计划，并取得适当器材及受训帮手作有支撑移动。路线及紧急程度应反映实际病情，而非平常辅助具。

00:21:45.768 --> 00:22:18.864
A safe transfer is a planned move, not simply a test of whether someone can stand. Assess current illness and injuries, mobility, strength, balance, ability to follow the plan, pain and fatigue, lines and tubes, weight-bearing restrictions, surfaces, route, equipment and trained help. A previous successful transfer does not establish current ability. Connect this to the CPSC assistance-level reading, while keeping assistance level and permission to load an injured limb as different questions.
安全转移是规划好的移动，不只是测试能否站起。应评估当前疾病及损伤、活动、力量、平衡、按计划配合的能力、疼痛与疲劳、管线、负重限制、表面、路线、器材及受训帮手。过去成功转移不证明目前能力。可连接CPSC协助层级阅读，但所需协助程度与伤肢是否允许承重，是不同问题。

00:22:18.864 --> 00:22:49.512
The visceral pleura covers the lung and the parietal pleura lines the chest wall. Their thin fluid interface normally helps couple lung movement to chest expansion. Air entering through a damaged chest wall or visceral pleura disrupts that relationship and permits lung recoil. Loss of ventilated lung can impair gas exchange. The source's small normal pleural-fluid volume is an anatomy reference, not a quantity to aspirate or a measure obtainable from the bedside examination.
脏层胸膜覆盖肺，壁层胸膜衬胸壁，两者之间薄液层通常有助于肺随胸廓扩张运动。空气通过受损胸壁或脏层胸膜进入后，会破坏这种关系，使肺回缩。有效通气肺面积减少可妨碍气体交换。来源的小量正常胸膜液是解剖参考，不是应抽出的量，也不是床旁检查能测得的量。

00:22:49.512 --> 00:23:22.464
Tension is a pressure-and-physiology problem, not merely a synonym for a large pneumothorax. Progressive intrathoracic pressure can compromise ventilation and venous return, producing obstructive shock. A large radiographic air space alone does not establish tension, and a smaller collection can become dangerous in the wrong physiology. Tracheal displacement may be late or absent; do not wait for it before recognizing a deteriorating patient and escalating through the applicable pathway.
张力性气胸是压力与生理问题，不只是大气胸的同义词。胸腔内压力持续增加，可妨碍通气及静脉回流，造成梗阻性休克。影像上气体范围大本身不确立张力，较小气体聚集在不利生理背景下也可危险。气管移位可较晚或缺如；不能等出现它才识别恶化并经适用路径升级。

00:23:22.464 --> 00:23:57.360
A chest drainage system collects output and limits reverse entry of air, using a water seal or another manufacturer-specific mechanism. The illustrated device has a marked collection chamber, an air-leak/water-seal area, suction control and a bellows indicator. These parts answer different questions: amount collected, air movement, selected suction and whether that particular suction mechanism is working. Identify the actual device and prescribed setup rather than assuming every drainage unit has the same chambers or controls.
胸腔引流系统收集流出物，并通过水封或其他厂家机制限制空气反向进入。图示设备有带刻度收集室、漏气或水封区、吸引控制及风箱指示。它们回答不同问题：收集量、空气移动、选定吸力，以及该具体吸引机制是否工作。应识别真实设备及规定设置，不能假设所有装置有相同腔室及控制。

00:23:57.360 --> 00:24:36.288
Suction is not automatically required for every chest drain. The textbook's blanket suction wording should be read against the actual order and device; selected BTS guidance does not advise routine initial suction for pneumothorax drainage. Likewise, bubbles must be interpreted by chamber, pattern, indication and device. Continuous air-leak bubbling is not made harmless simply because a pneumothorax was present. Assess the patient and system, preserve the authorized setup and escalate concerns instead of improvising clamping, disconnection or suction changes.
每条胸腔引流管不都自动需要吸引。教材的一概吸引措辞，应与实际医嘱及设备对照；BTS选定指导不建议气胸初始引流常规加吸引。同样，气泡必须按腔室、模式、适应背景及器材解释。不能只因有气胸就认为持续漏气气泡无害。应评估患者及系统，保留获准设置，并升级沟通担忧，不能即兴夹管、断开或改吸力。

00:24:36.288 --> 00:25:08.952
Hypovolemic shock is inadequate circulation associated with critical intravascular volume loss. Real blood loss can be external or concealed inside the body; the source's description of absolute loss as visible is too narrow. Vomiting, diarrhea, fistula drainage, sweating, osmotic diuresis or other excessive urinary losses can also reduce volume. Identify the actual loss and its mechanism rather than treating all cases as visible external hemorrhage.
低血容量休克是与血管内容量显著丧失有关的循环不足。真实失血可外显，也可隐匿在体内；来源把绝对丧失描述成可见，过于狭窄。呕吐、腹泻、瘘管引流、出汗、渗透性利尿或其他过多尿丧失，也可减少容量。应识别真实丧失及机制，不能都当作可见外出血。

00:25:08.952 --> 00:25:39.168
Reduced filling can lower stroke volume and cardiac output. Sympathetic responses may increase rate, contractility and vascular tone, temporarily preserving pressure while tissues remain threatened. Renal and hormonal responses conserve fluid over time. Compensation has limits and varies with age, medications, illness and injury; absence of marked tachycardia or hypotension does not exclude serious hypoperfusion.
充盈减少可降低每搏量及心输出量。交感反应可增加心率、收缩力及血管张力，在组织仍受威胁时暂时保留血压。肾脏及激素反应会随时间保留液体。代偿有限，并随年龄、药物、疾病及损伤变化；没有显著心动过速或低血压，也不能排除严重低灌注。

00:25:39.168 --> 00:26:12.816
Original case: a worker is struck on the left chest by a falling crate. There is little visible bleeding, but breathing is increasingly difficult, one side moves less and the worker becomes less responsive while the measured systolic pressure is still one hundred one. Assess and support the patient promptly, look for both impaired breathing and concealed loss, and request the appropriate resources. Do not wait for tracheal deviation or pressure below ninety, and do not assume that no visible blood means no volume loss.
原创情境：工人左胸被落下的箱子击中，少有可见出血，但呼吸越来越困难、一侧活动减少，并在实测收缩压仍为101时反应下降。应及时评估支持，同时寻找呼吸受损及隐匿丧失，并请求适当资源。不能等气管移位或血压低于90，也不能假设没有外显血液就没有容量丧失。

00:26:12.816 --> 00:26:45.672
Worked reasoning: pleural pressure can obstruct circulation, whereas bleeding can reduce the amount returning to the heart; both may occur together after chest trauma. The actual examination and trajectory determine concern, not one label or normal-looking number. Explain your findings, likely threats, interventions and response in the handover. A general textbook procedure or fluid paragraph does not expand PCP scope, and reassessment continues while definitive care is arranged.
推理示范：胸膜压力可梗阻循环，而出血可减少回心血量；胸伤后两者可能并存。应由实际检查及变化过程决定担忧程度，不是单个标签或看似正常数字。交接时解释发现、可能威胁、措施及反应。一般教材操作或补液段落不会扩大PCP权限；安排确定性照护时仍须继续复评。

00:26:45.672 --> 00:27:17.136
Begin with the target. Platelet activation and aggregation help build a plug; coagulation stabilizes it with fibrin. Antiplatelets reduce platelet activity, anticoagulants interfere with coagulation, and thrombolytics promote breakdown of fibrin through the enzyme plasmin. Aspirin is not a medicine that directly dissolves an established clot. The class name helps interpret a medication history, but it does not tell you every indication, bleeding risk or reversal plan.
先看作用目标。血小板激活和聚集帮助形成栓子，凝血过程以纤维蛋白加固。抗血小板药减少血小板活动，抗凝药干预凝血，溶栓药通过纤溶酶促进纤维蛋白分解。阿司匹林不是直接溶解既成血栓的药。类别有助理解用药史，却不能独自说明全部适应症、出血风险或逆转计划。

00:27:17.136 --> 00:27:53.760
P2Y12 is a platelet receptor for adenosine diphosphate. Clopidogrel requires metabolic activation, importantly involving CYP2C19; poor activation can mean less protection, not simply fewer side effects. Genetic variation and inhibitors such as omeprazole or esomeprazole can reduce its effect. Opioids can delay absorption of oral P2Y12 drugs. Recognize these history and handover issues without independently adding a loading dose, changing gastric treatment or stopping a prescribed antiplatelet.
P2Y12是血小板上的二磷酸腺苷（ADP）受体。氯吡格雷需要代谢激活，CYP2C19尤其重要；激活不足可能意味着保护不足，而不只是副作用少。遗传变异及奥美拉唑或埃索美拉唑等抑制剂可降低作用；阿片药可延迟口服P2Y12药吸收。应把这些作为用药史及交接问题识别，而不是自行追加负荷量、更改胃药或停用处方抗血小板药。

00:27:53.760 --> 00:28:31.056
Assess for visible and concealed bleeding: prolonged wound bleeding, black stools, blood in urine, coffee-ground vomit, hemoptysis, severe new headache or deterioration after a head injury. CBC, hemoglobin/hematocrit trends and platelet counts help in the hospital context, but a normal early value does not exclude a new bleed. Platelet number does not directly measure all platelet-function inhibition. Connect the medication history to injury mechanism, perfusion, mental status and repeated observations rather than looking for bruises alone.
应评估可见及隐匿出血：伤口久流、黑便、血尿、咖啡渣样呕吐、咯血、新发剧烈头痛，或头伤后恶化。医院中的CBC、血红蛋白或血细胞比容趋势及血小板计数有帮助，但早期正常值不能排除新出血；血小板数量也不直接测出所有功能抑制。要把用药史连到损伤机制、灌注、意识及反复观察，不能只找瘀青。

00:28:31.056 --> 00:29:06.528
Teach both sides of the risk: bleeding needs prompt evaluation, while premature discontinuation can increase thrombotic events, especially after coronary intervention. A generic five-to-seven-day preoperative sentence is not permission for a patient or field provider to choose a stop date; timing is agent- and procedure-specific and belongs to the treating team. Explain injury prevention, medication identification and what changes to report. Use a question such as, What would you do after a head injury even if the bleeding outside seems small?
教育须讲风险两面：出血需要及时评估，而过早停药可增加血栓事件，尤其冠脉干预后。泛称术前停五至七天，不允许患者或现场人员自行选停药日；时间取决于具体药及操作，应由治疗团队决定。要说明预防损伤、用药身份信息及需报告变化。例如可问：头伤后，即使外部出血很少，你应怎么办？

00:29:06.528 --> 00:29:39.288
Cardiac output is heart rate multiplied by stroke volume, with units of volume per time. For example, eighty beats per minute times sixty milliliters per beat equals forty-eight hundred milliliters per minute, or four point eight liters per minute. That is not the volume of one beat. The source four-to-five-liter resting reference is not a normality guarantee for every size, activity or illness. A fast rate can coexist with poor output if filling and stroke volume fall.
心排量等于心率乘每搏量，单位是体积除以时间。例如80次/分乘60 mL/次，得到4800 mL/min，即4.8 L/min，不是一次搏动的体积。来源静息4至5 L参考，并非所有体型、活动或病情都正常的保证。若充盈及每搏量下降，快心率仍可伴低心排。

00:29:39.288 --> 00:30:15.312
Preload concerns ventricular filling/stretch before contraction, afterload the load against ejection, and contractility the muscle response at a given loading state. Venous return influences preload but is not its interchangeable definition. Pressure can be related approximately to flow and resistance; it is not a direct ATP meter. Inadequate oxygen delivery or use can impair cellular energy and organs. Thus one medicine that raises pressure may not correct the cause, and excessive afterload can make a failing pump work harder.
前负荷涉及收缩前心室充盈或伸展，后负荷是射血需克服的负载，收缩力是一定负载状态下心肌的收缩反应。静脉回流影响前负荷，但不能把两者定义互换。血压可近似联系血流与阻力，却不是直接ATP仪。氧输送或利用不足可损害细胞能量及器官；因此升压药未必纠正病因，过大后负荷还可增加衰竭泵的负担。

00:30:15.312 --> 00:30:54.336
Four mechanisms organize shock: loss of effective circulating volume, failed pumping, obstructed filling/outflow, or inappropriate vascular distribution/tone. They can coexist. The source wrongly makes reduced vascular resistance sound like the necessary consequence of blood loss; sympathetic compensation can instead raise resistance while stroke volume falls. Distributive shock is not simply all fluid moving outside vessels. Think about flow, vascular tone, oxygen content and tissue use together; a preserved cuff pressure does not exclude shock.
休克可按四种机制组织：有效循环容量丧失、泵衰、充盈或流出受阻，以及血管分布或张力失调；多种机制可并存。来源错误地让血管阻力下降看似失血的必然后果；交感代偿反而可在每搏量下降时升高阻力。分布性休克也不只是全部液体移到血管外。应结合血流、血管张力、携氧量及组织利用；袖带血压尚维持不能排除休克。

00:30:54.336 --> 00:31:36.384
Volume loss requires cause control, such as stopping hemorrhage, alongside appropriate circulatory support and access to definitive care. Fluid is not equivalent to oxygen-carrying blood or hemostasis. Pump failure is different: large uncritical fluid loads may worsen pulmonary congestion. Obstruction is different again: a vasoactive drug does not remove tension physiology or tamponade. Current D01 calls for judicious fluid use and consultation in suspected cardiogenic shock. Identify mixed or uncertain shock and escalate rather than forcing every patient into one drug category.
容量丧失需要控制病因，例如止血，同时给予合适循环支持及确定性照护。补液不等同具有携氧功能的血液，也不等同止血。泵衰不同，不加判断大量补液可加重肺淤血；梗阻又不同，血管活性药不能移除张力生理或心包压塞。现行D01对疑似心源性休克要求谨慎用液及咨询。应识别混合或不明休克并升级，不能强把人人套进一种药类别。

00:31:36.384 --> 00:32:16.080
In anaphylaxis, vasodilation and leakage can impair circulation while airway swelling or bronchospasm impairs breathing. Epinephrine addresses several receptor-mediated problems; inhaled salbutamol addresses bronchospasm, not the whole syndrome. The current E09 initial IM pathway is distinct from advanced refractory IV care and arrest dosing. Do not delay indicated IM epinephrine for a perfect monitor setup or replace it with a nebulizer. Observe breathing, circulation and consciousness in parallel, and communicate whether the intended response occurs.
过敏反应中，血管舒张和渗漏可损害循环，气道肿胀或支气管痉挛可损害呼吸。肾上腺素针对多个受体介导问题，吸入沙丁胺醇针对支气管痉挛而非整个综合征。现行E09最初IM路径，不同于高级难治IV照护及骤停剂量。不能为完美监护配置延误有指征IM肾上腺素，也不能用雾化替代。应并行观察呼吸、循环和意识，沟通是否出现预期反应。

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:51.816
Albuterol is the US name used here for salbutamol. Its predominant beta-two action relaxes bronchial smooth muscle; tremor, tachycardia, dysrhythmia or paradoxically worse breathing can occur. Other sympathomimetics, beta blockers and some antidepressants can alter the response. Listen to air entry and observe work of breathing, rate, oxygenation and the patient, rather than declaring success because the nebulizer emptied. New chest pressure, marked palpitations or worsening distress needs reassessment.
这里美国名称albuterol对应salbutamol，即沙丁胺醇。其主要β2作用使支气管平滑肌放松，也可出现震颤、心快、心律失常或反常呼吸恶化。其他拟交感药、β阻滞剂及部分抗抑郁药可影响反应。应听进气，观察呼吸用力、频率、氧合及患者，而不是因雾化杯空了就宣布成功。新胸压、明显心悸或窘迫加重需要复评。

00:32:51.816 --> 00:33:31.512
Isotonic refers to effective osmotic behavior relative to plasma, not a promise that every isotonic solution has exactly the same sodium concentration as blood. Saline and balanced crystalloid differ in composition. The source gives rapid one-to-two-liter anaphylaxis and two-liter hypovolemia examples. Keep those hospital examples visible as source content, not fixed instructions for every adult, child, hemorrhage or congested heart. Use the cause-specific current service pathway, individualized response and overload reassessment; do not make finishing a bag the clinical goal.
等渗指相对血浆的有效渗透行为，不保证所有等渗液的钠浓度都与血液完全相同。盐水和平衡晶体液成分不同。来源有过敏性休克快速1至2 L、低血容量2 L示例；应明确这是医院来源内容，不是所有成人、儿童、出血或淤血心脏的固定指令。须采用病因特定现行机构路径、个体反应及过负荷复评，不能以输完一袋为临床目标。

00:33:31.512 --> 00:34:13.752
Norepinephrine, also called noradrenaline, stimulates adrenergic receptors; the prototype table heading alpha/beta antagonist is an error. Alpha-mediated vasoconstriction and beta-mediated cardiac effects can support selected hypotension, but the pulse does not always rise: reflex bradycardia can occur. A higher pressure can coexist with poor flow when volume is inadequate. The source statement no contraindications does not mean no precautions. Recognize ischemia, arrhythmia, excessive vasoconstriction, rebound hypotension after abrupt cessation and IV extravasation injury.
Norepinephrine又称noradrenaline，即去甲肾上腺素，激动肾上腺素能受体；原型表写alpha/beta antagonist是错误。α介导缩血管及β介导心脏效应可支持选定低血压，但脉搏不一定升高，也可有反射性心动过缓。容量不足时，血压升高仍可伴低血流。来源称无禁忌，不代表无注意事项。应识别缺血、心律失常、过度缩血管、突然停用后反跳低血压及静脉外渗伤害。

00:34:13.752 --> 00:34:49.296
Original Week 9 case: a maintenance worker falls from a platform and reports taking two tablets after a coronary stent, but cannot name them. There is chest pain, a painful swollen thigh, cool skin and increasing confusion. A coworker reports a recent missed dose. State the immediate assessment and hemorrhage-control priorities, how to verify the medicines without delaying care, and what the history adds to the handover. Neither a possible antiplatelet nor a missed dose establishes the single cause of deterioration.
原创第9周病例：维修人员从平台跌落，报告冠脉支架后服两种片剂，却说不出名字。患者胸痛、大腿痛且肿胀、皮肤凉及逐渐意识混乱。同事说最近漏过药。请说明即时评估及止血重点、如何不延误照护地核实用药，以及这些病史给交接增加什么。可能服抗血小板药或漏药，都不能证明恶化只有一个病因。

00:34:49.296 --> 00:35:32.688
Worked reasoning: trauma can cause concealed volume loss, impaired ventilation or obstruction, while coronary disease remains relevant. Assess actual breathing, pulse and perfusion; look for accessible bleeding and other time-critical injuries, arrange resources and conveyance, and report exact observations and uncertainty. Do not reflexively give nitrate for chest pain, a hospital vasopressor for one low pressure, or an extra antiplatelet to compensate for an unverified missed dose. Change only the later history to a recent head strike: concern for intracranial bleeding increases even if external bleeding is minimal.
推理示范：创伤可造成隐匿容量丧失、通气受损或梗阻，冠心病仍相关。应评估真实呼吸、脉搏及灌注，寻找能处理的出血和其他时间紧迫损伤，安排资源及转运，并报告准确观察和不确定性。不能因胸痛就反射性给硝酸甘油、因一次低压就给医院升压药，或为未经核实的漏药追加抗血小板药。若后来病史只改成近期撞头，即使外部出血少，颅内出血担忧也会上升。

00:35:32.688 --> 00:36:11.280
Trace the pulmonary loop aloud: systemic veins and coronary sinus to right atrium, tricuspid valve, right ventricle, pulmonary valve and trunk, right/left pulmonary arteries, smaller branches and alveolar capillaries. After exchange, pulmonary venules and usually four pulmonary veins return blood to the left atrium. Pulmonary arteries therefore normally carry relatively oxygen-poor blood and pulmonary veins relatively oxygen-rich blood. The bronchial systemic supply serves lung tissue itself and is not the same route as alveolar gas-exchange flow.
应能口述肺循环：体静脉及冠状窦至右房，经三尖瓣至右室，再经肺动脉瓣、肺动脉干、左右肺动脉、小分支到肺泡毛细血管。交换后，经肺小静脉及通常四条肺静脉回左房。因此肺动脉通常携相对缺氧血，肺静脉携相对富氧血。支气管的体循环供应服务肺组织自身，不等同肺泡气体交换血流路线。

00:36:11.280 --> 00:36:46.824
The usual arch has three major branches: brachiocephalic trunk, left common carotid and left subclavian. The right common carotid and right subclavian arise from the brachiocephalic trunk; do not invent a matching left brachiocephalic artery. Each subclavian supplies branches including vertebral, internal thoracic and thyrocervical pathways before continuing toward the arm. In contrast, both right and left brachiocephalic veins exist. Similar words do not make the arterial and venous trees mirror images.
常见主动脉弓有三个大分支：头臂干、左颈总动脉及左锁骨下动脉。右颈总及右锁骨下源于头臂干，不要虚构一条对称的左头臂动脉。各锁骨下动脉发出椎动脉、胸廓内及甲状颈干等路线，再向手臂延续。相反，左右头臂静脉都存在；词语相似不表示动静脉树是镜像。

00:36:46.824 --> 00:37:24.576
For the arm, follow subclavian, axillary, brachial, then radial and ulnar to palmar arches and digital branches. Radial follows the thumb-side radius; ulnar follows the little-finger-side ulna in anatomical position. Humeral circumflex, deep brachial and collateral branches serve shoulder, posterior arm and elbow regions along the way. The arches link channels in the hand; their presence does not guarantee an injured hand has adequate perfusion. This route explains why assessment above and below an injury answers different questions.
上肢依次追踪锁骨下、腋、肱，再到桡及尺，经掌弓至指分支。解剖位桡侧沿拇指侧桡骨，尺侧沿小指侧尺骨。旋肱、肱深及侧支沿途供应肩、臂后及肘区域。掌弓连接手内通道，但存在掌弓不保证受伤手灌注足够。此路线解释为何损伤近远端评估回答不同问题。

00:37:24.576 --> 00:38:01.488
For the leg, follow external iliac, femoral and popliteal, then anterior tibial to dorsalis pedis or posterior tibial to plantar supply. Deep femoral/circumflex and genicular branches serve thigh and knee territories; fibular or peroneal names refer to the same lateral-leg pathway. Resolve the source ambiguous pronoun with its own table: medial and lateral plantar arteries arise from posterior tibial, not from a fibular artery that simply splits into both. Dorsal and plantar anastomoses distribute blood toward toes.
下肢依次髂外、股、腘，之后胫前至足背，或胫后至足底供应。股深、旋股及膝分支供应大腿和膝区域，fibular与peroneal指同一腓侧路线。来源正文代词含糊，应结合自身表格澄清：足底内和外侧动脉来自胫后，不是腓动脉简单分成这两支。足背和足底吻合向足趾分配血流。

00:38:01.488 --> 00:38:34.752
Upper-body return usually reaches the superior vena cava through the paired brachiocephalic veins. Each brachiocephalic is formed mainly by internal jugular plus subclavian; external jugular usually drains into subclavian, while vertebral and internal thoracic tributaries also contribute. The two brachiocephalics unite into SVC, which receives the azygos arch and empties into right atrium. Coronary venous return through the coronary sinus is a separate route directly to that atrium.
上半身回流通常经成对头臂静脉至上腔静脉。每侧头臂主要由颈内与锁骨下汇成，颈外通常入锁骨下，椎及胸廓内等属支也参与。左右头臂合成SVC，接受奇静脉弓后入右房；心脏静脉经冠状窦则是直接至右房的另一路线。

00:38:34.752 --> 00:39:15.096
The hepatic portal route connects two exchange beds before general venous return: digestive/splenic capillaries, portal tributaries and vein, liver sinusoids, then hepatic veins and IVC. Superior mesenteric plus splenic commonly form the portal vein; inferior mesenteric often joins splenic, while gastric and cystic tributaries contribute. Hepatic arterial blood also reaches the liver. This arrangement supports nutrient handling and first-pass processing, but does not mean every swallowed substance is completely removed or that portal and systemic veins are interchangeable.
肝门路线在一般静脉回流前连接两个交换床：消化或脾毛细血管、门脉属支与门静脉、肝血窦，再到肝静脉和IVC。肠系膜上与脾静脉常汇成门静脉，肠系膜下常先入脾，胃和胆囊属支也参与；肝动脉血也到肝。此安排支持营养处理及首过过程，但不表示每种吞服物都完全清除，也不表示门脉与体静脉可互换。

00:39:15.096 --> 00:39:47.472
In fetal circulation, the placenta provides gas exchange. One umbilical vein brings relatively oxygen-rich fetal blood toward the fetus; two umbilical arteries return relatively oxygen-poor blood toward placenta. The fetal and maternal circulations exchange across the placental interface rather than normally forming one continuous shared blood pipe. Not all oxygenated umbilical blood bypasses the liver, and the fetal lungs still receive blood for growth even though they are not the main gas-exchange organ.
胎儿循环由胎盘承担气体交换。一条脐静脉把相对富氧的胎儿血带向胎儿，两条脐动脉把相对缺氧血带回胎盘。胎母循环在胎盘界面交换，正常并非连成同一条共用血管。不是所有富氧脐血都绕肝，胎肺虽非主要气体交换器官，仍接受生长所需血流。

00:39:47.472 --> 00:40:30.384
Know three shunts and their adult remnants. Foramen ovale permits right-to-left atrial flow and leaves the fossa ovalis; ductus arteriosus connects pulmonary trunk toward aorta and leaves ligamentum arteriosum; ductus venosus links umbilical return toward IVC while bypassing much hepatic exchange and leaves ligamentum venosum. After birth, lung expansion and lower pulmonary resistance increase left-atrial filling relative to right, helping close the atrial flap. Oxygen and circulatory changes promote ductal closure; functional and anatomical closure are not all instantaneous with the first breath.
应掌握三种分流及成人遗迹。卵圆孔允许右房至左房血流，留下卵圆窝；动脉导管连肺动脉干至主动脉，留下动脉韧带；静脉导管把脐回流引向IVC、绕过大部分肝交换，留下静脉韧带。出生后肺扩张及肺阻力下降，使左房充盈相对右房增加，有助瓣样开口关闭。氧及循环变化促进导管关闭；功能和解剖关闭并非全部在第一口气瞬间完成。

00:40:30.384 --> 00:41:21.240
Altitude lowers barometric pressure while the oxygen fraction remains about twenty-one percent. The source dry-air table pairs pressures of 760, 632, 565, 447, 350 and 260 millimeters of mercury with oxygen partial pressures about 159, 133, 118, 94, 73 and 54. These examples span sea level through roughly twenty-nine thousand feet. They are not arterial blood-gas values or saturation percentages. For example, twenty-one percent of 760 is about 160, whereas twenty-one percent of 447 is about 94; the fraction stayed similar while the pressure fell.
海拔上升使大气压下降，而氧比例仍约21%。来源干空气表把760、632、565、447、350、260 mmHg，分别配到氧分压约159、133、118、94、73、54，示例从海平面到约29,000英尺。这些不是动脉血气值，也不是饱和度百分比。例如760的21%约160，447的21%约94；比例相似而压力下降。

00:41:21.240 --> 00:41:59.832
Adaptation has different time scales. Ventilatory and acid-base responses occur early; reduced plasma volume can increase hemoglobin concentration without immediately making new red cells. EPO-mediated production contributes over longer exposure. Thus an immediate higher hematocrit is not proof that EPO already produced a new red-cell mass. Acclimatization reduces risk but is not guaranteed protection at a new higher sleeping altitude. Hydration supports ordinary needs; forced drinking is not a substitute for acclimatization, descent or treatment.
适应有不同时间尺度。通气和酸碱响应较早，血浆容量减少可在尚未立即制造新红细胞时提高血红蛋白浓度；EPO介导生成则在更长暴露中参与。因此即时血细胞比容升高，不证明EPO已经造出新的红细胞总量。适应可降低风险，但到更高睡眠海拔不保证受保护。补水支持一般需要，强迫饮水不能代替适应、下降或治疗。

00:41:59.832 --> 00:42:34.776
Original integration: at a high camp, a worker cuts a thigh on damaged equipment and later has increasing breathlessness and confusion. One finger saturation seems plausible for the altitude. Explain why that number cannot exclude concealed blood loss, impaired ventilation or altitude illness, and trace how a fall in venous return can reduce output. The immediate task is a coordinated assessment, hemorrhage control, environmental protection and resource/evacuation plan, not choosing a single reassuring measurement.
原创整合：高处营地工人被损坏器材割伤大腿，随后呼吸困难及意识混乱渐增，某指端血氧看似符合该海拔。请解释此数字为何不能排除隐匿失血、通气受损或高原病，并追踪静脉回流下降如何降低心排。即时任务是协调评估、止血、环境保护及资源和撤离计划，不能挑一个让人安心的数字。

00:42:34.776 --> 00:43:17.256
Worked explanation: the pulmonary loop loads oxygen, systemic arterial branches distribute blood, and venous routes return filling volume. A local injury and a lower inspired oxygen pressure can impair different parts of this chain simultaneously. Assess the whole patient and trends while addressing time-critical threats. For retrieval, draw one arm arterial route, one foot-to-heart venous route, the liver portal sequence and the three fetal shunts; then explain altitude using fraction versus partial pressure. The guide covers the assigned narrative domains and selected figures, not every optional link or source assessment.
推理示范：肺循环摄氧，体动脉分支分配血，静脉路线返回充盈容量。局部损伤与吸入氧分压降低，可同时损害链条不同部分。应处理时间紧迫威胁，同时评估整体患者及趋势。提取时画一条上肢动脉路线、一条足至心静脉路线、肝门顺序及三种胎儿分流，再以氧比例与分压解释海拔。本指南涵盖指定正文领域及选定图示，不包括每个可选链接或来源考题。
